{"duration_api_ms":94574,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"baac37ad-bd5f-4512-8a20-991dfe09304d","total_cost_usd":0.6221422,"usage":{"input_tokens":28,"cache_creation_input_tokens":37284,"cache_read_input_tokens":815891,"output_tokens":8029,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":787},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":37284,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1070,"cache_read_input_tokens":69041,"cache_creation_input_tokens":581,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":581},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":28,"outputTokens":8029,"cacheReadInputTokens":815891,"cacheCreationInputTokens":37284,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6221422,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":787,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":37284,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":14,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I recommitted the lock test, but the change still shows no measurable speed-up: the review's main demand, a gain beyond the run-to-run spread, isn't met. With twice the samples, time-to-ready is unchanged.\n\n**Lock test.** `.theseus/oracle/perf/comments-addnew-locks.cjs` is committed this time. It opens a document in the original build (A) and the changed one (B) and checks the Comments add button once the document has loaded:\n- it is in `lockControls`, in `paragraphControls` and in the Toolbar controller's `btnsComment`;\n- it is enabled after load, like the toolbar comment button;\n- it turns off and back on with that button under the lost-connection and paragraph locks.\n\nBoth builds give identical results: PASS. One surprise: `btnsComment` is on the Toolbar controller, not on the view.\n\n**Measurement.** 30 alternating A/B pairs × 2 documents (10 and 100 pages), up from 16, with no other factory agents running (load 2.0 before, about 5 at the end from the run itself). Deltas are B − A:\n\n| | median | middle half of pairs | B faster in | mean ± standard error |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Ready (editor ready) | −2 ms | −98 to +94 ms | 30 of 60 | −5 ± 21 ms |\n| LoadDoc (document load call) | −32 ms | −167 to +62 ms | 34 of 60 | −44 ± 21 ms |\n\nThe −40 ms Ready result from the previous attempt shrinks to about zero with more pairs. Any real effect is under roughly 40 ms, about 1.5% of a ~3 s open. LoadDoc leans slightly faster, but that doesn't carry through to Ready.\n\n**Decision.** I didn't change the code or the measurement to make a gain appear. The change does no harm, but it doesn't speed up opening either. I left keeping or dropping it to the reviewer and operator. The numbers and raw data (`perf/open-window-build-PKT-0132-2026-11-04-r3.json`) are in `baseline.md`, and the decision is in the Executor log.\n\n**Checks.** Both acceptance commands pass (the differential oracle on 4 cases). `theseus scope-check` is clean. `theseus validate` reports 0 errors and 4 warnings, which I didn't look into. The friction line is appended, and the work is committed as `bef4896`. Nothing new in `external/web-apps` this attempt: it stays at `59da4221`, which already has the lock fix.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- In the document editor, reading `buttonAddNew` from Comments forces the view to build. A late-wired button must copy its `keepState` and disabled state from `btnsComment[0]`, because `ButtonsArray.add` applies a stale flag.\n- 16 pairs gave a misleading −40 ms. Perf packets need about 30 or more pairs before claiming an effect.\n- Nothing in the method says what to do with a perf packet whose measured effect is zero; I noted this in the friction line.","ttft_ms":3291,"type":"result","duration_ms":760396,"uuid":"70fbcf43-0493-4047-88b0-edb9065c69a7","ttft_stream_ms":2794,"time_to_request_ms":325,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":234,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":16,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":6,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":9,"query_setup":4,"auto_mode_context_wait":5,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":16,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":6},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":12,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":127,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":210,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":138,"process_rss_mib_result":226,"process_anon_mib_result":135,"process_peak_rss_mib":261,"process_cpu_ms_turn":6392,"process_wall_ms_turn":760395,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":1137,"process_wall_ms_streaming":64275,"main_stream_count":14,"main_stream_event_count":1197,"main_stream_chunk_count":813,"process_turn_states":{"main_stream":{"cpu_ms":1137,"wall_ms":64275,"entries":14},"tool":{"cpu_ms":4014,"wall_ms":665282,"entries":13},"first_event_wait":{"cpu_ms":774,"wall_ms":30212,"entries":14},"before_first_request":{"cpu_ms":128,"wall_ms":325,"entries":1},"between_requests":{"cpu_ms":324,"wall_ms":289,"entries":13},"after_last_request":{"cpu_ms":15,"wall_ms":12,"entries":1}},"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_o